speechtext:
My hon. friend from Oxford, the ex-parliamentary secretary to the Secretary of State for External Affairs, intervenes. I am sure he knows that what I am saying is right. If he were the
Supply-External Affairs parliamentary secretary to the Secretary of State for External Affairs-and he is not;
I do not know why he is not-and he were in that role tonight, I would not object to his beginning a discussion, because after all he has had four years experience at the United Nations while my hon. friend the parliamentary secretary to the Minister of Finance has been engaged in matters having to do with financial policy. If this request is not granted in spite of the repeated and earnest requests put forward by my two colleagues and myself, what will be the result?
